## Under the types (root TypedApp): `U8.to(start, 3)`'s first argument is a
## U8 by the checker (`start = 0`, the literal the call makes one), and
## `Iter.fold`'s an Iter, so all three calls are proven; but
## `start.to(3).fold(...)` leaves `start`'s type to default, and the one
## confirm fails. (A constant numeric expression is no candidate; a name
## bound to one is, and only the compiler or an expect sees it.) The file
## goes back to rounds: the line's two calls stay, with the compiler's
## reason, and the other is still turned.
ProvenFails := [].{
	bytes : List(U8)
	bytes = {
		start = 0
		Iter.fold(U8.to(start, 3), [], |acc, b| acc.append(b))
	}

	size : List(U8) -> U64
	size = |b| b.len()
}

expect ProvenFails.size(ProvenFails.bytes) == 4
